Actually for calico, the arm7 default image `ds7_maine.elf` is linked in by default when using `-7 arm7/elementia.elf`. Let me just write a minimal ARM7 main using the calico API:

```c
#include <nds.h>
int main(void) {
	irqInit();
	touchInit();
	irqSet(IRQ_VCOUNT, vcountCallback);
	irqEnable(IRQ_VCOUNT);
	touchStartServer(0, 3);
	fifoInit();
	soundInit();
	while (1) swiWaitForVBlank();
}
```

Hmm, but `touchStartServer(lyc, prio)` — with libnds 2.0 the server runs in a thread. Let me check what the combined template does. Let me list the combined template files.

